Third-party data attributions (free/open sources — wired adapters + planned catalog)
================================================================================
BEACON consumes only free, open, license-compatible data. Attribution is required
by several sources and is reproduced here (and surfaced in-app via provenance).

45 sources have a wired adapter. This is machine-verifiable, and was re-verified
on 2026-09-16: `config/adapters.json` (45 rows) and the typed `ADAPTER_FACTORIES`
map in `src/main/adapter-registry.ts` (45 entries) are an EXACT id-for-id
match — firms, nws, nwps, glofas, gdacs, meteoalarm-ro, meteoalarm-gr,
meteoalarm-es, wmo-swic, open-meteo, usgs-water, gdelt, reliefweb, agency-rss,
bluesky, mastodon, nifc, effis, osm-overpass, worldpop, census, nfhl, eagle-i,
opencellid, itu, camara-gsma, caltrans-cctv, alertwildfire, windy-webcams,
dot511, cnadnr-ro, metno, anm, hdxpop, hifld, eonet, cemsrm, openfema, caphub,
lanceflood, nri, openaq, airnow, sensorcommunity, shelters-fema. All 45 are attributed below.

"Wired" here means the adapter exists and its port registration is validated at
boot. WHICH of the 45 are additionally CONSUMED by the live COP/map composition
is a separate question with a single authority — docs/audit/DATA_SOURCE_VERIFICATION.md
§0 — and is deliberately not restated in this file. Four are known NOT to be
consumed: `itu` and `camara-gsma` (operator-gated MOCK-only plugins by design),
`hifld` (registered but HELD out of every region's allowlist pending a
merge-not-replace slot design — its static 2019 snapshot displaces the seeded
infrastructure the outage derivation depends on) and `dot511` (covers Georgia
only). Attribution is reproduced for all 45 regardless, since a MOCK/CACHED rung still carries the upstream
provider's recorded data.

The "Not-yet-wired" entries further below are attribution-reserved for genuinely
planned adapters (`config/planned-sources.md`) and are NOT consumed by the running
app at all. Each is listed with its compatible license.

